## Changing the environment

`env` is required. Set it to a concrete environment for an environment-specific gate or to `"*"` for a gate that applies to all environments. A gate with `env = "*"` cannot coexist with environment-specific gates for the same service and identifier. Evaluations still use a concrete environment. Monitor queries are not automatically changed to match the evaluation environment.

Changing `env` replaces this resource. With Terraform's default destroy-before-create lifecycle, replacing one gate deletes it and its rules before creating the replacement and its rules. Evaluations can have no matching gate during this interval. `create_before_destroy`, including when inherited from another resource, instead attempts to create the new gate first and fails if it conflicts with the old gate. Remove conflicting gates or choose a new identifier before applying.

Replacing one resource does not coordinate deletion of other environment-specific resources. To consolidate several gates with the same service and identifier into one all-environments gate, first remove all conflicting environment-specific gates and apply. Then add the `env = "*"` gate and its rules in a second apply. This leaves an evaluation gap until the new gate and its rules are ready. If evaluations must continue during migration, create the all-environments gate with a new identifier first, update evaluation callers to use it, and then remove the old gates.

